# Trivy misconfiguration baseline.
#
# Everything NOT listed here fails the gate, so this file is a record of
# accepted findings - not a way to turn scanning off. Each entry names the TODO
# item that will remove it, or the ADR that makes it deliberate.
#
# Re-check with:
#   trivy config --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --skip-dirs .terraform .

# SQS queues are not encrypted with a KMS key. 12 queues.
# Real finding. Tracked as TODO §5.4.
# Note for whoever fixes it: enabling encryption also requires kms:Decrypt /
# kms:GenerateDataKey on the IoT topic-rule role (producer) and on all three
# ECS task roles (consumers). AWS-managed keys (alias/aws/sqs) have no key
# charge, only API-call charges.
AWS-0096

# SNS topics are not encrypted. 2 topics.
# Real finding. Tracked as TODO §5.4.
AWS-0095

# The shared security group allows unrestricted egress (0.0.0.0/0, all
# protocols). Real finding. Tracked as TODO §5.9 - it needs a full test cycle
# before tightening, because the services reach IoT, SQS, DynamoDB, SSM,
# CloudWatch, ECR and SES.
AWS-0104

# Subnets associate a public IP address on launch.
# DELIBERATE, not a defect - see docs/adr/0001-public-subnets-and-gateway-endpoints.md.
# The tasks have a zero-ingress security group, so there is no inbound path;
# the public IP exists purely so egress works without a NAT gateway. Changing
# this would add fixed ongoing cost for no security gain.
AWS-0164

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- image CVEs
# Both are build/packaging tools bundled inside python:3.11-slim, not runtime
# dependencies of these services - the containers only ever import boto3.
# Neither is cleanly fixable: `pip install --upgrade pip setuptools wheel` was
# tried and produced FOUR fixable CVEs instead of two (it dragged in newer
# urllib3/msgpack/setuptools issues), so the upgrade was not adopted.
# They clear when the base image rolls forward - Dependabot tracks the docker
# ecosystem for exactly that.
CVE-2026-23949
CVE-2026-24049